    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of pairwise games for a single team:**\n   Each team plays 3 games with each of the other 8 teams. Therefore, the number of games played by one team is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ games/team} \\times 8 \\text{ other teams} = 24 \\text{ games}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of unique pairings of teams:**\n   We need to choose 2 teams out of the 9 to play a game. The number of ways to choose 2 teams from 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of teams and \\( k \\) is the number of teams to choose at a time:\n   \\[\n   \\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of games:**\n   Since each pair of teams plays exactly one game, the total number of games is the number of ways to choose 2 teams to play from 9:\n   \\[\n   36 \\text{ games}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the baseball league is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{36}\n\\]",
